				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Sole-writer-per-derivation\n\nEach derived state has exactly one cache that owns it. The cache subscribes once to the raw input, recomputes, and emits narrow events for downstream consumers. Consumers don't touch the input event; they listen on the cache's outputs. Heavy work happens once, cheap re-rendering happens N times.\n\nThe `Flow` view on {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleSourceCache}} below paints this concretely: input event (yellow) flows into the cache (pink, sole subscriber), which fans out two narrow output events (yellow) to its consumer classes (gray). The two caches we built are {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleResolution}} (singleton, \"is this module loaded?\") and {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleSourceCache}} (per-module, source + function entries)."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T17:19:13.028036+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T17:19:13.028036+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "lUWqVMU3TquUFqnco9WTqg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleResolution}}, the loaded-module cache\n\nA class-side singleton holding two `Set`s: `resolved` (BEAM-confirmed loaded) and `unresolved` (BEAM-confirmed not loaded). Names in neither set are `#unknown`. {{gtMethod:name=BeamModuleResolution>>classify:}} is what the wrench styler asks; truly-unknown names get batched into one `Analysis.modules_loaded?/1` bridge call rather than one round-trip per name.\n\nIt subscribes weakly to `BeamModuleRecompiled` on the wildcard channel and additively moves the named module from `unresolved` to `resolved` on each event. No invalidation, no follow-up bridge call. Inspect the singleton to see what's in each set right now:"
			},
