				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Two consumers, two events\n\nThe `Flow` view above shows the cache emitting two narrow events. The two consumers wire as follows:\n\n- {{gtClass:name=ElixirModuleCoder}} listens on {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleEntriesUpdated}} (coarse, fires once per recompile) and primes its `cachedFunctionEntries` ivar in {{gtMethod:name=ElixirModuleCoder>>onBeamModuleEntriesUpdated:}}, then republishes a local `GtCoderSourceCodeChanged` for module-wide consumers (Source tab, Functions tab list).\n- {{gtClass:name=ElixirFunctionExpanderAttribute}} listens on {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleSourceChanged}} (narrow, per (function, arity)) and filters to its own coordinates in {{gtMethod:name=ElixirFunctionExpanderAttribute>>onSourceChanged:}}. Most events are no-ops for any given expander.\n\nThe example below saves HotReloadTest and asserts the coder ivar got primed."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "pharoSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:48.127518+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
