				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "HhsaKbmmRhiNMzxwo39z5A=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Weak subscriptions\n\nEvery subscription uses `weak when:send:to:` so closed inspectors and GC'd coders don't pin themselves alive. Watch the Fanout view to see this directly: close a coder, run `Smalltalk garbageCollect`, refresh the view, the receiver count drops.\n\nBloc elements with non-trivial work on each event (e.g. {{gtClass:name=ElixirCoderBrowser}}'s sidebar fan-out) additionally subscribe in `onAddedToSceneGraph` and unsubscribe in `onRemovedFromSceneGraph` so background browsers stay silent. The browser's handler is pure invalidation: drop `rawNodes`, let the next user interaction refetch lazily. That keeps a save fan-out from triggering 50+ round trips per browser."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T17:19:58.84156+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T17:19:58.84156+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "wjR8/ff4RkGq9hTHoNrnug=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Stale-proxy detection\n\n`BeamProxyObject`s in cached entries carry `elixirVar` IDs that point at slots in the prior session's `GtBridge.ObjectRegistry`. After a BEAM restart those slots no longer exist. {{gtMethod:name=BeamModuleSourceCache>>entries}} probes `entries first attributeAt: #name`; nil triggers a `clear` so the next consumer read goes through a bridge fallback rather than rendering `nil/nil` rows."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
