				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Bridge-restart lifecycle\n\nBoth caches subscribe idempotently (via `class >> initialize`) to `LanguageLinkStartAnnouncement` on `LanguageLinkApplication announcer`. When the BEAM bridge restarts:\n\n- {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleResolution}} drops its singleton (`reset`). The `resolved`/`unresolved` sets the prior session classified are no longer authoritative.\n- {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleSourceCache}} walks `liveCaches` and calls `clear` on each, *keeping the registry intact*. Consumers (`ElixirFunctionExpanderAttribute`, `ElixirModuleCoder`) hold the cache instance strongly via `sourceCache` ivars; dropping the registry would orphan those instances while the next `for:` built a fresh one, and both would process recompile events so consumers would see every event twice.\n\nThe next consumer read of an instance finds an empty cache and falls back through the bridge call that returns fresh proxies."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
