				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## BEAM-side mirror\n\nThe same pattern lives on the BEAM side in `GtBridge.Events` via the EventBroker library. `%ModuleEvent{kind: :recompiled, mod: ..., source_hash: ...}` fans out to subscribers like `GtBridge.CacheReaper` (invalidates the per-module ETS cache) and `GtBridge.Xref` (replaces the module's call-graph entries). The HTTP response carries the same `recompiled` payload list to GT, where {{gtMethod:name=ElixirModuleCoder>>announceBeamRecompiledFrom:}} hands it to {{gtClass:name=BeamEventAnnouncer}}.\n\nLive regression coverage: {{gtClass:name=BeamEventBusExamples}} has 17 examples covering announcer dispatch, per-module routing, payload propagation, cross-coder sync, Source/Functions tab refresh, and the browser-invalidation path. Each one runs from the inspector."
			}
		]
